================================================================================
MINIMAL FIX FOR CS DiD SIMULATION NULL SIZE FAILURE
================================================================================

PROBLEM:
  Type I error rate = 0% (should be ~5%)
  All simulations fail with error: "argument 'y' is missing, with no default"

ROOT CAUSE (verified with A/B tests):
  est_method="ipw" with xformla=~1 (no covariates) fails in did package
  IPW propensity score estimation requires non-empty covariate matrix
  With xformla=~1, fastglm() receives empty design matrix and throws error

EVIDENCE FROM A/B TESTS (N=500 sims each, synthetic data):
  - est_method="reg": reject_rate = 4.8%, sd_z = 1.019 ✓ NOMINAL
  - est_method="ipw": FAILS with fastglm error ✗
  - bstrap TRUE vs FALSE: No difference (both ~4%)
  - cband TRUE vs FALSE: No difference (both ~4%)
  - FE on untreated vs all data: No difference (both ~4%)

CONCLUSION:
  The ONLY cause of the 0% rejection rate is est_method="ipw"
  All other factors (bootstrap, cband, FE fitting) are irrelevant

================================================================================
THE FIX (ONE LINE)
================================================================================

FILE: power_simulation_cs_statepanel_staggered_parallel_merged.R
LINE: 155

FROM:
  did_method <- getenv1("DID_EST_METHOD", "ipw")

TO:
  did_method <- getenv1("DID_EST_METHOD", "reg")

RATIONALE:
  - Regression adjustment works with xformla=~1
  - IPW requires covariates to estimate propensity scores
  - With no covariates, IPW fails
  - REG directly models outcomes without propensity scores

ALTERNATIVE FIXES (not recommended):
  1. Add covariates to xformla (requires covariate data)
  2. Use est_method="dr" (doubly robust, slower)
  3. Fix fastglm to handle empty covariate matrix (requires did package change)

